# Workato Documentation and Corporate Site

> Workato is the enterprise automation and integration platform powering the agentic enterprise. Workato ONE is built on four pillars: Workato Agentic (design, deploy, and orchestrate AI agents), Enterprise MCP (give agents the context and trust to act across your enterprise), Workato Orchestrate iPaaS+ (integrate apps, data, processes, and APIs at enterprise scale), and Universal Connectivity (connect every system — from modern SaaS to legacy mainframes, LLMs, databases, and data lakes). Trusted by over 10,000 organizations including Atlassian, Broadcom, and leading Fortune 500 companies.

## Platform Overview

- [Workato ONE Platform](https://www.workato.com/platform): The cornerstone platform page for Workato ONE — covers the full product suite, four platform pillars, enterprise infrastructure capabilities, and Workato's positioning as the trusted foundation for mission-critical agentic orchestration.
- [What is Workato](https://docs.workato.com/getting-started/what-is-workato.html): Documentation introduction to Workato's unified platform — core concepts, how recipes, connectors, and agents work together, and the federated governance model.
- [Agentic Product Suite](https://www.workato.com/agentic): Overview of Workato's full agentic product suite — Workato Agentic, Enterprise MCP, Agent Studio, Genies, and Agent Orchestration — in one place.
- [Product Hub](https://www.workato.com/product-hub/): Release notes, product updates, and feature announcements across the Workato platform.
- [2025 Product Highlights](https://www.workato.com/product-hub/2025-product-highlights/): Summary of all major product capabilities and releases launched in 2025.

