## Documentation and Developer Resources

### Getting Started

- [Workato Docs Home](https://docs.workato.com/): Full product documentation covering recipes, connections, connectors, security, APIs, administration, and agentic capabilities.
- [Getting Started with Workato](https://docs.workato.com/getting-started/what-is-workato.html): Beginner-friendly introduction to the platform — key terminology, how recipes and connectors work, and how to build your first automation.
- [Workato Concepts](https://docs.workato.com/workato-concepts.html): Core concepts and terminology across the Workato platform — workspaces, projects, recipes, connections, triggers, actions, and data pills explained.
- [Developer Sandbox](https://www.workato.com/developers/sandbox): Sign up for a free developer sandbox to build and test integrations and agentic workflows in an isolated environment before going to production.

### Recipe Design and Automation

- [Recipes Overview](https://docs.workato.com/recipes.html): What recipes are, how they work, and how they form the backbone of all automations on the Workato platform.
- [Building Recipes](https://docs.workato.com/recipes/building-recipes.html): Step-by-step guide to designing recipes — adding triggers, configuring actions, applying logic, and testing before deployment.
- [Triggers](https://docs.workato.com/recipes/triggers.html): How triggers work in Workato — polling, real-time, scheduled, and event-based triggers across connected apps and systems.
- [Steps and Actions](https://docs.workato.com/recipes/steps.html): How to configure actions within recipes — create, update, search, and delete operations across connected apps with conditional logic and looping.
- [Process Automation Guide](https://docs.workato.com/process-automation.html): Deep-dive into building multi-step automations including conditional logic, looping, error handling, and orchestrating complex business processes.
- [Data Pills and Field Mapping](https://docs.workato.com/recipes/data-pills-and-mapping.html): How to map and transform data between steps in a recipe using Workato's data pill framework — the foundation of all data handling in recipes.
- [Jobs and Run History](https://docs.workato.com/recipes/jobs.html): How Workato processes trigger events as jobs, monitors execution history, and surfaces logs for debugging and auditing.
- [Error Handling Best Practices](https://docs.workato.com/recipes/best-practices-error-handling.html): Strategies for managing errors in recipes — monitoring for failures, preventing invalid operations, sending alerts, and using handle-errors blocks.

### Data Transformation and Formulas

- [Formulas](https://docs.workato.com/formulas/other-formulas.html): Workato's formula library — allowlisted Ruby methods for transforming strings, numbers, dates, arrays, and objects within recipe steps.
- [Lookup Tables](https://docs.workato.com/features/lookup-tables.html): Create and use lookup tables within recipes to map values, enrich data, and resolve static reference data without external API calls.

### Connections and Connectors

- [Connections](https://docs.workato.com/connections.html): How Workato authenticates and manages connections to business applications — auth methods, connection scopes, and how connections are reused across recipes.
- [Community Recipe Library](https://docs.workato.com/community-library.html): Browse and install pre-built recipes, connectors, and skill recipes contributed by the Workato community.
- [Salesforce Connector Docs](https://docs.workato.com/connectors/salesforce.html): Full documentation for the Workato Salesforce connector — triggers, actions, supported objects, real-time events, and bulk operations.
- [HubSpot Connector Docs](https://docs.workato.com/connectors/hubspot.html): Full documentation for the Workato HubSpot connector — contact management, deal workflows, marketing automation triggers, and API v3 support.
- [OpenAPI Connector](https://docs.workato.com/connectors/openapi/): How to use the Workato OpenAPI connector to integrate any REST API with an OpenAPI specification — no custom connector code required.

### API Platform

- [API Platform Overview](https://docs.workato.com/api-management.html): Full-lifecycle API management built into Workato — build, publish, secure, and monitor APIs entirely in the cloud with recipe-backed endpoints.
- [API Platform Key Features](https://docs.workato.com/features/api-management.html): API gateway, federation, developer portal, and policy enforcement — how Workato's API management layer works for internal and external API consumers.
- [Create an API Recipe](https://docs.workato.com/api-mgmt/api-recipes/walkthrough.html): Step-by-step walkthrough for building recipe-backed API endpoints — configure request/response schemas, authentication, and rate limiting.
- [Workato API — Introduction](https://docs.workato.com/workato-api.html): Overview of the Workato platform API — programmatic access to recipes, connections, jobs, and workspace management.
- [Workato API — Resources](https://docs.workato.com/workato-api/resources.html): Complete reference for all Workato API resources — agent studio, API clients, connections, connectors, data tables, jobs, recipes, projects, and lifecycle management.
- [Workato API — Recipes](https://docs.workato.com/workato-api/recipes.html): API endpoints for managing recipes programmatically — list, create, start, stop, and retrieve recipe details via the Workato REST API.

### Custom Connector Development

- [Custom Connector Builder](https://docs.workato.com/developing-connectors/custom-connector.html): Build custom connectors for proprietary or niche applications using Workato's no-code custom connector tool — no SDK required for straightforward REST APIs.
- [Connector SDK](https://docs.workato.com/developing-connectors/sdk.html): Full Workato Connector SDK documentation — build, test, and publish production-grade connectors using Workato's Ruby-based SDK with custom auth, triggers, and actions.

### Agentic Documentation

- [Agent Studio — Agent Orchestration](https://docs.workato.com/en/agentic/agent-studio/agent-orchestration.html): How to configure agent orchestration in Agent Studio — enabling Genies to run multi-step tasks autonomously within recipes, including decision-making, data gathering, and document handling without user input.

### Administration and Lifecycle

- [Recipe Development Lifecycle](https://docs.workato.com/recipe-development-lifecycle/rdlc-guide-planning.html): Planning and managing recipe lifecycle from development through testing to production — version control, environment promotion, and governance best practices.

## Integrations Library

> Workato connects to more enterprise applications than any other automation platform, with over 1,200 pre-built connectors spanning ERP, CRM, HRIS, and financial systems. Each integration page documents pre-built triggers, actions, and recipe templates for that connector. All connectors are included in every Workato plan — no per-connector fees.

- [Full Integration Library](https://www.workato.com/integrations): Browse all 1,200+ pre-built connectors organized by category — SaaS apps, databases, data warehouses, LLMs, on-prem systems, and more.

